WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
A small firm has ten people.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:07.160
Its job advert boasts: average
salary, sixty thousand pounds.

3
00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:11.510
But nine of the ten staff earn
twenty-five thousand pounds each.

4
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.870
Is the boss lying?

5
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.800
Or can an average really be more than
twice what nine in ten staff earn?

6
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.630
In this mission, you'll
find the mean, median,

7
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.480
mode and range of a set of data.

8
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.110
You'll work out averages
from frequency tables,

9
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.760
using running totals.

10
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.990
And you'll learn how to choose the
average that best fits the data.

11
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.750
Your mission: explain how the average
pay can be sixty thousand pounds.
